# cage is the usual host compositor (`cage -s -mlast -- regreet`); sway or
# Hyprland work too. glycin-loaders + bubblewrap decode the background image.
Recommends:
 cage | sway | hyprland,
 glycin-loaders,
 bubblewrap,
Description: clean and customizable GTK 4 greeter for greetd
 ReGreet is a graphical greeter for the greetd login daemon, written in Rust
 with GTK 4 and Relm4. It lists users and X11/Wayland sessions, remembers the
 last user and session, and can be themed with a background image, GTK
 settings and CSS.
 .
 It needs a Wayland compositor to run in, usually cage. Configure it in
 /etc/greetd/regreet.toml and /etc/greetd/regreet.css, and point greetd's
 default_session at it.
